  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 210 AM EDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\n- Mostly Sunny into Tuesday\n\nPressure heights increase as the mid level ridge moves overhead\nalong with the surface high. Mostly sunny skies and light winds\nare expected. A lake breeze develops this afternoon with westerly\nwinds pushing inland. Winds will be more southwesterly Tuesday\nahead of our next chance for rain.\n\nHighs in the mid 70s to mid 80s are expected with lows in the 50s\nwith a couple spots north of US-10 potentially dropping into the\nupper 40s.\n\n- Showers and Thunderstorms Possible Tuesday Night into Friday\n\nA broad upper level trough moves in mid week with heights\nbeginning to lower Tuesday night. Overall showers Tuesday night\nmay remain just north and west of the forecast area until better\nforcing and moisture moves in Wednesday morning. The trough axis\nand surface front will be slow moving in and out of the area. A\nlull in showers is possible Wednesday afternoon before another\nround of positive vorticity advection moves through Wednesday\nnight into Thursday morning. Instability is limited, mean values\naround 500 J/kg or less, and shear is weak. Therefore the\npotential for severe thunderstorms is low. Dry conditions slowly\nmove in Thursday night into Friday behind the front.\n\nThere is the potential for shower and thunderstorm chances to\nlinger into the weekend looking at ensembles. Within the broad\ntrough in southwest to west flow we do not clear out the\ninstability and moisture in the area. However confidence is not\nhigh enough to add PoPs into the forecast this far out. With no\nsignificant source of lift, most if not all could remain dry.\n\nTemperatures will continue to be in the 70s to 80s during the day\nwith overnight lows in the 50s and 60s.",
